# Speaking Portfolio System Requirements

## Purpose

The Speaking Portfolio System allows students to upload speaking recordings, review AI-generated transcripts, edit transcripts, and submit them for assessment.

The system provides teachers with tools for grading, reviewing audio, viewing transcripts, and exporting participation metrics.

---

# Functional Requirements

## Authentication

### FR-001

Users shall authenticate using Microsoft 365 credentials.

### FR-002

The system shall support the following roles:

- Student
- Teacher
- Administrator

---

# Student Requirements

### FR-101

Students shall be able to view assignments assigned to them.

### FR-102

Students shall be able to select partners.

### FR-103

Students shall be able to upload audio recordings.

Supported formats:

- MP3
- M4A
- WAV

### FR-104


The system shall generate a transcript after upload.

Acceptance Criteria:

- Student receives a transcript after audio upload.
- Transcript is editable.
- Transcript is stored with the submission.
- Transcript can be regenerated by the teacher if necessary.


### FR-105

Students shall be able to edit the generated transcript.

### FR-106

Students shall be able to submit the final transcript.

---

# Teacher Requirements

### FR-201

Teachers shall be able to create classes.

### FR-202

Teachers shall be able to import students using CSV.

### FR-203

Teachers shall be able to create assignments.

### FR-204

Teachers shall be able to grade submissions.

### FR-205

Teachers shall be able to export results as CSV.

---

# Administrator Requirements

### FR-301

Administrators shall manage teacher accounts.

### FR-302

Administrators shall view all classes.

### FR-303

Administrators shall export institution-wide results.

---

# Metrics Requirements

### FR-401

The system shall calculate word count from the final transcript.

### FR-402

The system shall calculate turn count.

A turn is defined as:

- One line of text
- Lines separated by Enter key presses

### FR-403

The system shall calculate average words per turn.

Formula:

Average Words Per Turn = Word Count / Turn Count

Rounded to two decimal places.

---

# Reporting Requirements

### FR-501

Teachers shall be able to export:

- Student Name
- Student Email
- Assignment Name
- Word Count
- Turn Count
- Average Words Per Turn
- Grade

Format:

CSV

---

# Performance Requirements

### FR-601

The system shall support at least 800 students.

### FR-602

The system shall support approximately 7,200 submissions per academic year.

### FR-603

The transcript generation process should begin returning results within 10 seconds when technically feasible.

---

# Technology Constraints

Preferred technologies:

- SharePoint Online
- SharePoint Lists
- SharePoint Document Libraries
- Power Automate
- SPFx
- React

Preferred authentication:

- Microsoft 365

Preferred storage:

- SharePoint

Preferred deployment:

- SharePoint-hosted solution

